   "gap_before": 0.75,
   "block": "books.dlg32",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then a paperback might actually be more thoughtful. She'll really use it.",
   "est_sec": 3.82,
   "gap_before": 0.48,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg32"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "But a hardcover looks nicer wrapped.",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.52,
   "block": "books.dlg32",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "True. You could do the paperback and write a little note inside the cover. That makes it feel personal.",
   "est_sec": 5.99,
   "gap_before": 0.85,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg32"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "A note. Yeah. She'd keep that forever.",
